<%#
  Purchase controls: the quantity stepper and the priced add-to-cart button.

  Expected locals:
    priceAud       — the product's price, for the button's label.
    priceFormatter — an Intl.NumberFormat, passed in so one price never renders
                     two ways on the same page.

  Every control is disabled: there is no cart yet, and `disabled` already keeps
  them out of the tab order, so nothing else is needed to stop the block
  offering something the site cannot do. It becomes real with the cart
  iteration.
%>
<div class="purchase">
  <div class="quantity">
    <button type="button" disabled title="Coming soon" aria-label="Decrease quantity"
      class="quantity__button">−</button>
    <span class="quantity__value">1</span>
    <button type="button" disabled title="Coming soon" aria-label="Increase quantity"
      class="quantity__button">+</button>
  </div>

  <button type="button" disabled title="Coming soon"
    class="button button--solid purchase__submit">
    Add to cart — <%= priceFormatter.format(priceAud) %>
  </button>
</div>
